Both P1 defects are fixed in the scratch worktree. No commits were made. No tests were run locally, per the execution constraint.

Changed [macro.cljc](/tmp/cc1-p1/src/cljc/yin/vm/macro.cljc) and added pins in [clojure_callsite_test.cljc](/tmp/cc1-p1/test/yang/clojure_callsite_test.cljc).

Fix summary:

- P1-1 reassembly: the prelude collection ops are now provenance-aware. Decomposition registers packet lineage by rows-object identity. Reassembly reattaches the retained origin only when root matches and every row is `identical?` to the registered packet's rows. Content twins recover nothing, so ruling U1 holds. Unaccounted children answer a missing marker. The expander refuses such outputs as `:missing-provenance` instead of fabricating `:constructed`.
- P1-1 child insertion: constructed packets delegate through the recovered child origin. The correspondence, walk, and side table now read retained origins correctly.
- P1-2 literal encoding: values entering `:data`/`:key` slots are stripped of only `:yin.vm.macro/origin-of`, recursively through elements, keys, values, and metadata. Legitimate user metadata is preserved. Stripping was chosen over moving tracking fully outside the value because direct pass-through already threads provenance on packets correctly. The defect was only the data-slot boundary.

New pins cover `repack`, reassembled-child insertion, and `packet-data`. They assert retained correspondence, source origins, recorded expansion origins, and clean literal encoding.

